  "id": "COMPOUND:19235 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-6-[2-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-5,7-dihydroxy-4-oxochromen-6-yl]-3,4,5-trihydroxyoxan-2-yl]methyl (E)-3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)prop-2-enoate] is implicated in the regulation of the Glucagon receptor through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of several compounds, including Chloramphenicol acetyltransferase, which in turn is a target of other molecules such as Galacturonic Acid and 2-[(3S)-3-hydroxy-2-oxo-1H-indol-3-yl]acetic acid. These latter compounds are also targets of 18,19-Dihydroangustine, which further supports the notion that the compound may interact with the Glucagon receptor through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where the compound may influence the Glucagon receptor via a chain of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with some pathways showing slightly higher scores, but the overall relationship is supported by multiple independent targets.",
